  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Backend",
      "items": [
        "Queries JPL Horizons: Sun/Earth az-el per site, Moon el per DSN site",
        "Curated sites and custom coordinates, no login",
        "Horizons responses cached on disk for <3 s answers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Web delivery",
      "items": [
        "Dokploy builds the Docker image from main",
        "nginx serves the Astro site behind Traefik"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Web app",
      "items": [
        "One time store (live, scrub or play) and one site store, shared by every view",
        "Views show the simulator's own sky at once (VENT-36: Sun, Earth, DSN from @ventana/sim) and Horizons when it arrives; a Data source switch picks Computed, Horizons or Compare",
        "Five languages (VENT-35): a static page per locale with hreflang, one catalogue each, Intl for numbers and dates; a lint rule and a parity test keep every string in all five",
        "MVP: calendar, polar map, site card; luxury: globes",
        "Built: the 3D globe (lazy-loaded, its Sun follows the instant, the selected site ringed, its state in the phone's site pill and a LOLA relief thumbnail, 1x and 2x, rendered offline by site_thumbs.py and committed, in the phone sheet and the desktop site card), the calendar strip, the site card, the polar map (header tabs by hash, keep the site and the instant) and the phone sheet with its calendar, all under one glass gate (Liquid refraction on capable Chromium, frosted elsewhere); one request per site and month (the month and its next 30 days), cached in the page",
        "Installable (VENT-28): a manifest per locale with the J2 icon and site shortcuts, a live favicon with the Moon's phase and the site's state, and a service worker (build-versioned cache, pages and API network first) that opens the app offline with its last data",
        "VENT-10, VENT-37: a pin, dropped by a click (or a held finger) on the globe or the polar map and dragged to adjust, makes any point the selected site (?lat&lon), answered at once by the simulator and then by Horizons",
        "Globe layers (VENT-37): a registry of layers (id, z, visible) the globe mounts; landing sites, zones and the sites saved on this device are layers, switched from the Layers key and kept on the device; API for other teams in docs/globe-layers.md",
        "DSN mode (VENT-7): the simulator finds each handoff between Goldstone, Canberra and Robledo to the minute, once per UTC day; a «Listening on Earth» block in the desktop card and the phone widget (small Earth seen from the Moon, real terminator, «No link» first when the Earth is under 3°) and a DSN view (#dsn, phone tab) with the big Earth, the Moon above 10° ring and the 24 h band following the shared instant",
        "On-foot 3D view (VENT-34, #horizon and the phone's Horizon tab, lazy-loaded, first person only since VENT-54): relief in rings from the aligned levelled tiles of /api/v1/terrain/tiles through a RingSource seam (VENT-46; a Web Worker streamer replaces it later), the far horizon from the point's profile, the Sun and the Earth at the shared instant, illustrative fine detail captioned; the API gzips its JSON",
        "Texture worker (VENT-101): the globe's 2K and 4K colour and the on-foot Earth ship as KTX2 (ETC1S); a worker of its own runs three's Basis transcoder under a CSP of its own, so the GPU holds 4 bits per texel, with the JPEG as fallback"
      ]
    }
  ]
